  "title": "Kirby Problem 4.8",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let X be a closed, simply connected, smooth 4-manifold, and T a smoothly embedded torus in X with $\\pi_{1}(X$ −T) =1 and $[T]^{2}$ =0. Let $X_{K}$ be the result of Fintushel–Stern knot surgery on X along a knot K. If $K_{1}$ and $K_{2}$ are two prime knots such that $X_{K,1}$ and $X_{K,2}$ are diffeomorphic, does it follow that $K_{1}$ is either $K_{2}$ or its mirror?",
